      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion in the same loop or domain",
      "functional_impact_measured": "Fluorescent \u03b1-bungarotoxin labelling confirmed surface display; BBS-\u03b32 enhanced AMPAR function identically to unmodified \u03b32 (AMPAR-enhancing function preserved); labelled \u03b32 co-localised with AMPAR clusters at synapses in living neurons.",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "rationale": "L1 reports a tolerated BBS insertion 'within the extracellular domain' of full-length CACNG2, a Type I TARP with topology identical to CACNG3; both proteins share the same large EC1 loop (TM1\u2013TM2) as their sole substantial extracellular domain. No specific residue is named in the paper, so insert_after_residue is left null and the site is reported at region level (EC1, CACNG3 residues 31\u2013105). The evidence is indirect (ortholog), so position_evidence is 'inferred' and confidence is medium; the validation level reflects what was actually measured in CACNG2 (surface display and preserved function). BBS (bungarotoxin binding site, ~13 aa) was inserted into the extracellular domain of full-length, membrane-anchored TARP \u03b32 (CACNG2/stargazin), the prototypical TARP and closest characterised ortholog of CACNG3. Both are Type I TARPs sharing identical 4-TM topology; the 'extracellular domain' in this context is the large EC1 loop (TM1\u2013TM2, residues 31\u2013105 in CACNG3). The tagged construct was expressed in neurons.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 39209103,
          "citation": "PMID 39209103",
          "claim": "We inserted the bungarotoxin binding site (BBS) within the extracellular domain of TARPs to enable their detection in cells exposed to fluorescent \u03b1-Btx. Focusing on the prototypical TARP \u03b32, we demonstrate that the small size of fluorescent \u03b1-Btx allows it to bind to the BBS-tagged TARP when associated with AMPARs. Importantly, labelled \u03b32 enhances AMPAR function in the same way as unmodified \u03b32. In living neurons, fluorescent \u03b1-Btx-labelled \u03b32 associates with AMPAR clusters at synapses."
        }
